#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:78
#: 09dd20db2d9b4711972e8da2fe4e7b33
msgid "A message will be displayed on the GCS and in the flight log whenever the fuel cell status changes.  The vehicle can only be armed when the fuel cell is reporting a status of 'Running'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:82
#: 405a4e9b64384650bf47002064f32ad2
msgid "Failsafes and Pre-Arm Checks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:84
#: 308109087b444286b550b74d89acabbd
msgid "Failsafes and pre-arm checks are hard-coded and based on the error codes sent by the fuel cell.  Failsafes have been separated into two groups: Low and Critical.  The error code groups are listed below.  If an error code is received from the fuel cell, the resulting failsafe action will be set by the :ref:`BATTX_FS_LOW_ACT <BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>` and :ref:`BATTX_FS_CRT_ACT <BATT_FS_CRT_ACT>` respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:87
#: d40f04a670c74f48a3d5acc3a2046387
msgid "Monitoring of the fuel cell's internal error codes for pre-arm checks and failsafes are only done on the battery monitor instance allocated for the electrical telemetry.  The electrical battery monitor instance must therefore be set to trigger failsafes based on error codes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:91
#: 5815a08c6eae4898b3cec02b2cf43653
msgid "Failsafe Low Action Error Code Group"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:138
#: 32c92616f98c43608019080ecbe4bf5d
msgid "Failsafe Critical Action Error Code Group"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:170
#: 7e706aeac6734e54bd098ec80a0a95f2
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:171
#: fe793d00de394252bf5324c802c3faf9
msgid "This example has been provided to make it clear how the failsafe actions are set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:173
#: e41b034072814dcbabb20d5fe0aaf84b
msgid "The battery monitors have been configured so that electrical telemetry data is on battery monitor 1 and hydrogen tank telemetry is on battery monitor 2:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:175
#: eb6e7fd13edd4b959a2b8bf41f8997c8
msgid ":ref:`BATT_MONITOR <BATT_MONITOR>` = 17 (electrical data)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:176
#: 3bfc8d86429541cd832380d1199d22cd
msgid ":ref:`BATT2_MONITOR <BATT2_MONITOR>` = 18 (tank data)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:178
#: 14d9406cddc741cd964e3aa078aaf271
msgid "The failsafe actions that correspond to the error code groups listed above are then set on battery monitor 1 as that is the one associated with the electrical telemetry data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:180
#: dc3813da2c844f6e87fbd8af7c480bca
msgid ":ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT <BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>` = 2 (RTL)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:181
#: 4a80917f0336454a8f141201e14f97b2
msgid ":ref:`BATT_FS_CRT_ACT <BATT_FS_CRT_ACT>` = 1 (land)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:183
#: 3d4c0f49e6c74557abdafdcff38019b0
msgid "A tank level failsafe has been set on battery monitor 2 so that the vehicle will return to land when the fuel level gets below 20%.  This is done by setting:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:185
#: 67cb583b4be046fa94635d4aa2bc6d04
msgid ":ref:`BATT2_FS_LOW_ACT <BATT2_FS_LOW_ACT>` = 2 (RTL)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:186
#: b32e1dfb00aa427587dd3b4e42934ff4
msgid ":ref:`BATT2_CAPACITY <BATT2_CAPACITY>` = 100"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:187
#: 6c8317599a054b94babdf2b6568b24b6
msgid ":ref:`BATTX_LOW_MAH <BATT_LOW_MAH>` = 20"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:189
#: 60335437eb164e30bc7ad4c5d8c56b9e
msgid "As previously mentioned, normal voltage failsafes can be used on this fuel cell model.  Hence, as a final belt-and-braces approach a critical voltage failsafe has been set on the electrical generator monitor instance to initiate an immediate landing if voltage gets to 3.3 V per cell:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie24-fuelcell.rst:191
#: 885ef8cf58b546e2be9056f6f6c286d4
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CRT_VOLT <BATT_CRT_VOLT>` = 39.6"
msgstr ""

